win32u, winevulkan: Vulkan for 32-bit programs

dlls/winevulkan/vulkan.c, dlls/winevulkan/vulkan_private.h
- A command pool's handle is the address of the program's own structure. A 32-bit program
  stores it without the base of its memory window (0043), and the Unix side used the number
  as an address: vkCreateCommandPool faulted. It gets the base now.

dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
- Mapped device memory of a 32-bit program is refused when its address is above 4 GB. The
  program's memory is a window above 4 GB here, so the test is whether the mapping is inside
  the window. (The memory itself comes from VK_EXT_external_memory_host, which MoltenVK has:
  Wine allocates it in the program's address space and Metal uses it in place.)

With both, Wine's Direct3D runs on its Vulkan renderer in a 32-bit program
(WINE_D3D_CONFIG=renderer=vulkan): tests/runtime/d3d9-draw.c passes as a 32-bit program.

diff --git a/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c b/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
index 3265d74..e3216d9 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
@@ -1196,7 +1219,14 @@ static VkResult win32u_vkMapMemory2KHR( VkDevice client_device, const VkMemoryMa
     }
 
 #ifdef _WIN64
+#if defined(__APPLE__) && defined(__aarch64__)
+    /* FineWine 32-bit: the program's memory is a window above 4 GB; a mapping inside it is one
+     * the program can reach. */
+    if (NtCurrentTeb()->WowTebOffset && res == VK_SUCCESS &&
+        (((UINT_PTR)*data ^ __wine_wow_window_base) >> 32))
+#else
     if (NtCurrentTeb()->WowTebOffset && res == VK_SUCCESS && (UINT_PTR)*data >> 32)
+#endif
     {
         FIXME( "returned mapping %p does not fit 32-bit pointer\n", *data );
         device->p_vkUnmapMemory( device->host.device, memory->obj.host.device_memory );
